(Track B3: pre-size reads from regular files.

 Read an 8193-byte regular file - deliberately not a power of two - into an
 empty dynamic buffer. With pre-sizing the buffer is grown once to st_size+1
 (8194) before the first read, so length equals the file size, capacity is
 exactly file_size+1, and the bytes match.)

(Create an 8193-byte temp file by writing a 1-byte chunk 8193 times.)
open a file for writing called wf at "./test_b330.txt".
a buffer called chunk is "A".
a number called i is 0.
While i is less than 8193,
  Write chunk to wf,
  i is i plus 1.
Close wf.

(Read it into an empty dynamic buffer.)
a buffer called dyn is "".
open a file for reading called rf at "./test_b330.txt".
Read from rf into dyn.
Close rf.

Print "length:".
Print dyn's size.
Print "capacity:".
Print dyn's capacity.
Print "first:".
Print byte 1 of dyn.
Print "last:".
Print byte 8193 of dyn.

Delete the file "./test_b330.txt".